{
  "dom_id": "step-q23926",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The surface area of a cube is $150$ square units. Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
  "worked_solution": "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made up of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{S}{6}=\\frac{150}{6}=25\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{25}=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $5$ units.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
